### Authentication & user management
### Routes: /api/auth/*
###
### Auth is OPTIONAL. When SCHIST_AUTH_ENABLED=false (default) every endpoint is
### open and the login flow is unnecessary. When enabled, protected endpoints
### expect an `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>` header (see {{authToken}} below).
###
### Real passkey login can't be driven from a .http file (WebAuthn needs a browser
### authenticator). Use passkeys.http to register/authenticate in the browser, then
### POST /auth/login/passkey here with the resulting credential id to mint a JWT.

@username = admin
@credentialId = REPLACE_WITH_CREDENTIAL_ID
@inviteToken = REPLACE_WITH_INVITE_TOKEN

### Is first-time setup required? (public)
# @name setupRequired
GET {{apiUrl}}/auth/setup/required
# => 200 { "requires_setup": true|false }

### Create the first user (public, only works while no users exist)
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/setup/first-user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "credential_id": "{{credentialId}}"
}

### Create a user from an invite token (public)
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/setup/invite-user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{inviteToken}}",
  "username": "invitee",
  "credential_id": "{{credentialId}}"
}

### Log in with a registered passkey credential id -> returns a JWT (public)
# @name login
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/login/passkey
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credentialId": "{{credentialId}}"
}
# => 200 { "token": "...", "user": {...} }
# Chain the token into protected requests via {{login.response.body.token}}.

### Current authenticated user (requires auth)
GET {{apiUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Generate an invite link for onboarding a new user (requires auth)
# @name invite
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/invite
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
# => 201 { "token": "...", "invite_url": "..." }

### Log out (public, stateless — client just drops the token)
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/logout

### List all users (requires auth)
GET {{apiUrl}}/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Create a user directly (requires auth)
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "editor",
  "is_admin": false,
  "credential_id": "{{credentialId}}"
}

### Delete a user (requires auth)
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/auth/users/editor
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
